ymbols, groups of symbols are in fact a single symbol- the Temple would have little meaning without the Scroll and the Sword, and the Bull must come with the Mistress of Honey. Those symbols gain meaning only when they come together, and as such should be coupled as a single symbol in the storyline. Other conspiracies will have their own symbols- the MM, for example, have the Pope, Blood and the original book after which they are named. The KoSG have Dragons, Royalty, The Name Which Shall Not Be Written and the Faceless Angels. The Hototogisu has Cuckoos, thievery and contracts, the AO have the djinn, prophecy and the Cults of the Phoenix and Set and Cheiron, of course, have their logo and centaurs. <br /> <br /> And that's it- combine those features together and you'll get a good basis for a Sovereignty for your chosen conspiracy!<br /> <br /> <br /> I've always assumed that while Cheiron are scary and do terrible things, the powers behind the conspiracy are not &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; or malicious. They have the theme of healing running through them all across the conspiracy, and it makes sense they came to &amp;quot;heal humanity&amp;quot;, and their Vigil uses monster parts in order to do so. In my head canon, their biggest enemy is the Contagion, which they came to heal. I've detailed my version for them in my Igniting the Fire fan supplement. For a more malicious Sovereignty where a powerful cooperation takes over the supernatural world and binds all monsters through capitalism and submit the whole world for its will, I'll look for the Hototogisu, who are far darker IMO than Cheiron, even if they put a nicer facade.<br /> <br /> As for the KoSG- I didn't finish watching Naruto so while I more or less know what happens there, it didn't really crossed my mind. I've just thought about what kind of world would they try to accomplish, and the result was, as you said, terrifying. </div> </div> </div> </div>Dude I really appreciate this. I generally keep my games at a mid tier level in terms of changes wrought upon the world, but I've been wanting to give the opportunity for big endgames when it comes to Hunter.<br /> <br /> Also I actually am quite the same way with chieron when it comes to whether they are malicious or not. Their practices suck in the current, and they truly are corporatism to the extreme, but I feel like it makes sense they'd want SOMETHING altruistic, as they go through the trouble of making actual medical miracles when they can","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T11:08:08-08:00","id":1503829,"title":"","content":"Updated on the <b>Vigil Ascended?</b><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}